    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Echo is a cinematic puzzle-adventure set in a world fractured by time.</strong><br>Play as a lone traveler navigating strange environments, guided only by echoes of distant voices \u2014 each with its own personality, agenda, and truth.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Harness a unique time-slowing ability to solve dynamic platforming puzzles, uncover hidden paths, and reveal the secrets of a world that remembers everything you've done \u2014 and everything you haven't.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Time-based puzzles</strong> that challenge your logic and creativity</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Internal voices</strong> echo your journey \u2014 wise, sarcastic, and analytical</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Six chapters</strong>, each in a distinct world inspired by ancient myths and sci-fi</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>No hand-holding</strong> \u2014 learn mechanics naturally by experimenting and failing</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Third-person exploration</strong>, cinematic moments, and surreal traversal mechanics</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/98a9e6fabdb0304f50d54bf24c042e76.poster.avif?t=1755004411\" width=414 height=232 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/98a9e6fabdb0304f50d54bf24c042e76.webm?t=1755004411\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/98a9e6fabdb0304f50d54bf24c042e76.mp4?t=1755004411\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Leap into the unknown</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With the double-jump unlocked, vertical puzzles shift \u2014 it\u2019s no longer about where you land, but when you commit.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/5295ee15e30d2952d920f99cf2457f2d.poster.avif?t=1755004411\" width=416 height=234 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/5295ee15e30d2952d920f99cf2457f2d.webm?t=1755004411\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/5295ee15e30d2952d920f99cf2457f2d.mp4?t=1755004411\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Ledge Catch After Jump</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Some paths don't lead forward. They fall beneath you.</strong><br>Mastering ledge grabs turns a near-miss into momentum.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/20c884f3e0738b34e019dd94373fdc88.poster.avif?t=1755004411\" width=420 height=230 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/20c884f3e0738b34e019dd94373fdc88.webm?t=1755004411\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/20c884f3e0738b34e019dd94373fdc88.mp4?t=1755004411\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Environmental Button Activation</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One step changes everything.</strong><br>Pressure plates shift the terrain itself \u2014 opening new paths, revealing truths, or collapsing the familiar.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/e24673cfdf7acea24b99a23af253c38e.poster.avif?t=1755004411\" width=414 height=232 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/e24673cfdf7acea24b99a23af253c38e.webm?t=1755004411\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/e24673cfdf7acea24b99a23af253c38e.mp4?t=1755004411\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A Story About Time, Perspective, and Identity</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At the heart of Echo is a question:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>What if your greatest strength was the ability to pause time \u2014 not to escape, but to listen? </i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3822650/extras/ead15c43ccb452b7200e45900f196d0f.avif?t=1755004411\" data-has-big width=800 height=528 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
